split cmd on linux is used to split the file in different chunck's of data

split -b 10k data.file

-b is the flag which is used to define the block size

The naming of the file will be xab,xcd...

split -l n data

where -l is the flag indicating the line 

n is used to represent number of line's

split -l n datafile -d -a 4 split_file

where -d is the flag which is used to more arguments (additonal argument's)



